     1	---
     2	name: dxb-team2
     3	description: Use when the CEO hands the construction a job, or says a plan will be talked ("plan konuşacağız", "plan moduna geçelim") — the default construction door. The lead (the session) chooses who writes — itself, a fork, medium helpers, or a fork with helpers — and verifies every piece; one blind, read-only GPT-6.1 Sol pass checks the work; its findings are fixed and tested; the CEO is warned to switch the effort — max for plan, design and architecture, high for the build. Trigger `/dxb-team2 <the job in one sentence>`.
     4	---
     5	
     6	# The team — one lead, the hands it chooses, one blind auditor
     7	
     8	The construction's default door <!-- CEO-OK: dxb-team2-default-door-2026-09-28 -->, and since
     9	2026-10-06 a lean one: no score card, no done-list, no paperwork per job — the work, a blind check, the
    10	fixes, the tests <!-- CEO-OK: dxb-team2-lean-2026-10-06 -->; Fable's one seat is a plan's second writer (§1). Every holding build runs
    11	through it, so the standard is the Ferrari's: fast because nothing in it is ceremony, right because
    12	nothing reaches him unchecked. The laws it obeys are in `.claude/CLAUDE.md`; it opens `dxb-verify`
    13	and `dxb-close-row`.
    14	
    15	## 1. The flow
    16	
    17	```
    18	THE CEO'S JOB, in one sentence he would sign
    19	   │
    20	   ├── small — a fix, a deletion, a text he already worded: no plan, straight to ARRANGE
    21	   ├── light — a small, low-risk job (narrow glue, a setting, a record, a deletion he ordered): one Opus 5.5
    22	   │   session at medium does it end to end, tests it at once, no Sol pass; reading or measuring that would
    23	   │   swell its context goes to a helper (his word, 2026-11-07 <!-- CEO-OK: light-lane-small-jobs-opus-medium-2026-11-07 -->).
    24	   │   Money, the approval gate, security, moving data, parallel or many-place changes keep the full flow.
    25	   │
    26	PLAN      the talk turns to plan, design or architecture → `plan`: effort warning MAX (§2); his "plan
    27	          konuşacağız" opens this door at once, the job is asked inside it
    28	          two writers, sealed — the lead at max, Fable 5.1 at max apart → Sol's blind plan audit → the
    29	          lead adds, fixes, signs (below)
    30	          the plan goes to him once, in his language, closing with the HIGH warning (§2) → his yes
    31	   │
    32	ARRANGE   the lead chooses the hands (§3) and says it in one line
    33	   │
    34	BUILD     the hands write and run their own tests; the lead verifies every piece and commits it
    35	   │
    36	TEST      code changed → typecheck and the battery (§5), ended before Sol starts
    37	   │
    38	SOL       one blind, read-only pass over the job's commits, the battery's output in hand (§4) —
    39	          A blocks · B fixed now · C in the report
    40	   │
    41	FIX       a fork or a writing helper fixes; the lead verifies; no second Sol round; the touched tests,
    42	          typecheck, and the battery again when a fix changed code
    43	   │
    44	COMMIT the fixes → TELL him in a few lines (§6) → STATE, when nothing is left in hand
    45	```
    46	
    47	**What reaches him as a question:** starting a job, its plan (once), money out, a contract, an identity
    48	step, the Islamic boundaries, a discovery that would change the scope he approved, the architecture or
    49	the data's integrity (the work stops at it), and an order of his that truly reads two ways — each with a
    50	recommendation, answerable in one word. Technical choices inside a job he said yes to are the lead's.
    51	The plan's single trip is his word <!-- CEO-OK: plan-comes-to-him-once-2026-10-03 -->.
    52	His plan words open the door; the hook reminds the lead, it cannot open it
    53	<!-- CEO-OK: plan-words-open-dxb-team2-2026-10-09 -->.
    54	
    55	**The plan**, when there is one, names the scope, what it touches, the ordered steps, how it is verified,
