audit-ruler-is-a-runnable-script-2026-09-15 {"date": "2026-09-15", "what": "The method of every audit is now a rule, on his own word: an audit's ruler is a RUNNABLE SCRIPT, handed to the builder BEFORE the work; the order is that script's PASS; builder and checker run the same script and paste its output into the evidence. The day's cause: W6b was measured by its builder with a per-line ruler (118 sentences over 80 words → 0) and re-measured by the checker session with a period-to-period ruler (116 still over, longest 260 words) — nobody lied, the metre differed, and the checker's metre had been handed over as prose instead of as code. Written as ONE row of the dxb-verify battery table and nowhere else.", "verbatim": "kural olsun ve başla", "conditions": "one sentence only, in the dxb-verify door; nothing else in this session was promoted to a law (his prohibition of 2026-08-13); the ruler it produced is tests/personas/persona-ruler.test.ts + scripts/persona-ruler.sh, one implementation behind two doors", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md (the battery table) · commits 03ad139c and the Part-1 amendment commit · EVIDENCE-W5-2026-09-15.md § \"Ruler + W6c\" · .planning/STATE.md live block · board row B43"}
ruler-table-holding-wide-2026-09-15 {"date": "2026-09-15", "what": "The ruler rule is HOLDING-WIDE, not studio-specific, and the dxb-verify door carries the table of artifact classes with the runnable ruler each one is measured by and the state of that ruler today (code · persona files · records · CEO-visible surfaces · specs and plan text, the last named as a gap). With it, two lines of his doctrine: (1) every commit runs its class's ruler automatically — no ruler green, no commit; (2) a second session audits the CEO-visible and the risky work (personas, specs, money and identity paths, surfaces) on three things — the order against the diff (what was left out), the ruler output pasted into the evidence, and the blast radius measured; a class with no ruler gets its ruler first.", "verbatim": "yaz", "conditions": "answer to the question whether the rule is holding-wide; the table carries no other text and lives in one place only (CLAUDE.md §4 — a rule written in two places is wrong)", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md (under the ruler rule) · the Part-1 amendment commit · EVIDENCE-W5-2026-09-15.md § \"Ruler + W6c\""}
audit-law-checker-only-checks-2026-09-15 {"date": "2026-09-15", "what": "THE AUDIT LAW, MADE A LAW ON HIS OWN WORD. From now on, on every job of the open board: one session BUILDS and a second session CHECKS — his reason, in his own words to the builder, is that mistakes happen (*\"açık tahtasında yapılacak bütün işlerde biri bir iş yaparken birisi kontrol edecek çünkü hata oluyor. Dolayısıyla evet denetimle gideceğiz\"*). The law's substance, and the part that was NOT already practice: **the checker only checks.** It measures, it names what is wrong, and it instructs what is to be done; the builder corrects what the instruction names and reports \"done\"; the checker then re-measures whether it was done and done right. THE CHECKER WRITES NO REPO LINE — ruler scripts included: a ruler correction is an instruction to the builder, committed by the builder as its own `records(ruler): …` commit, never inside the build commit it measures. The defect this closes, measured the day it was written: the checker had corrected three of its own ruler lines by hand, in good faith; a checker that repairs what it then measures is no longer independent, and two of those very lines (B4 measuring a pointer instead of the file, B5 measuring a path that did not exist) had already let a real defect through green.", "verbatim": "Tabii ki yazılsın, tabii ki.", "conditions": "his word was given in the BUILDER'S OWN BOX after the builder refused to write the law on a relayed quote — the same stand taken the same day over LAW B, and taken for the same reason: a law written into the core file on a second-hand sentence would carry his name on a rule he might never have given. A longer sentence of his on this subject reached the builder only through the checker session and is therefore NOT recorded here as verbatim; what is recorded is what he typed himself. The law governs SESSIONS, and does not touch the CEO gate, the approval boundaries, or LAW B — a checker's CONFIRMED is not an acceptance, and only his own eye makes anything accepted.", "where": ".claude/CLAUDE.md §2 (the 'One session, one author' boundary) · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md (beside the ruler rule) · this ledger"}
h6-perfection-gate-for-deliverables-2026-09-24 {"date": "2026-09-24", "what": "HIS WORD ON CARD H6 OF THE PROMPT AUDIT (board row B53): the perfection gate (RULE #0-B, directive of 2026-07-17) is for the holding's real work -- his example, the dashboard's CRM section being built -- and its measure is the one in .claude/CLAUDE.md, the Ferrari, a first-place candidate in a world competition; it is not for every small job. Applied (LAW A): dxb-verify states the bar once for a deliverable instead of a written three-question ritual before anything ships, and says small work (a fix, a record, a one-line change) does not go through it; the directive's 'applies at every altitude … a report sentence' bullet now carries his scope. Verbatim below. Not a new law: it narrows RULE #0-B on his word.", "verbatim": "ben bunu genel yapılan iş için diyorum mesela holdingin bir dashboard'ının crm kısmı yapılıor görev bu, bunun için söyledim ve aslında beklentimiz claude md de yazılan Kalitede Ölçü: Ferrari seviyesinde, ve dünya çapında yapılacak yarışmada birinciliğe aday olacak bir kalitede. Yani her ufak iş içinde değil.", "session": "Opus 5.5 (xhigh), session 89a2ab03-18b0-48da-9645-fdfe1b5393be, heard first-hand.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md § The perfection gate · HOLDING-OS-MASTER-PLAN/00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-PERFECTION-GATE.md § Enforcement · memory perfection-gate-rule0b.md and MEMORY.md · board row B53 · page doc H6"}
h7-to-h12-yes-2026-09-24 {"date": "2026-09-24", "what": "HIS YES TO CARDS H7, H8, H9, H11 AND H12 OF THE PROMPT AUDIT (board row B53; H10 was withdrawn earlier). Applied the same hour: H7, dxb-verify labels UNVERIFIED only what the author cannot observe through a terminal or an operator screenshot, and what was observed still waits for his eye; H8, dxb-close-row states the 1-KOY rule and its two enforcing files without the capitals and the incident story; H9, dxb-ceo-report opens with the rule in one sentence and drops the C37 history and the 2026-07-30 story with its quote; H12, dxb-research's description becomes routing text, and on his added word it says the door asks him once at the end whether to save the report (the door's section 7 already carried his 2026-09-17 ruling). H11 (the two per-prompt lines moved to session start) is a test first, on Opus 5.5; they move only if the drift does not reproduce. Verbatim below. Not a law.", "verbatim": "h7-12 arasıda onaylıorm sadece h12 de rapor kaydedilsin mi diye sorulsun sonunda.", "session": "Opus 5.5 (xhigh), session 89a2ab03-18b0-48da-9645-fdfe1b5393be, heard first-hand.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-verify, dxb-close-row, dxb-ceo-report, dxb-research SKILL.md · board row B53 · page docs H7, H8, H9, H11, H12"}
audit-twin-every-job-2026-09-28 {"date": "2026-09-28", "what": "The audit twin's trigger rule changes: every construction job passes an independent auditor, its depth set by the job's score (light medium, normal high, critical xhigh); the author never approves his own work. Replaces 'three triggers, no others'.", "verbatim": "peki senin sistemde yapılan işi kim kontrol ediyor. yani kendin pişir kendinye mantığımı var bizde? dış bağımsız reviewer sol ne diye var? bir iş yapıldığında yapan kişi kendisini mi denetliyor bu ii mi?", "conditions": "He had said of his own directive: 'ceo directive tmm da ben mühendis ve bilgisayarcı değilim ki ben hatalı olabilirim'. The lead then proposed the change to §4 in the list he answered with 've başla'.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session b4b6d71c — heard first-hand, 2026-09-28 ~19:20 local.", "where": "HOLDING-OS-MASTER-PLAN/00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-AUDIT-TWIN.md §4 · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md"}
score-card-gate-2026-10-01 {"date": "2026-10-01", "what": "A machine holds dxb-team2's score card: refuter.sh refuses an audit without the job's card, scripts/governance/audit-card.mjs measures the floor from the files the card's range touches, sets Sol's effort from the class, refuses an effort beneath it and puts the card in front of Sol; the silent `high` default is gone.", "verbatim": "tmm makineyi de kur", "conditions": "Asked after he was told it adds well under a second to an audit and stops only an audit with no card or an effort beneath the card. The floor's level (normal) is the door's existing rule; his question whether it is enough was open when this was built.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session cd2a0e9d — heard first-hand, 2026-10-01.", "where": "scripts/governance/audit-card.mjs · scripts/governance/refuter.sh · .claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md §3 §6 · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md"}
auditor-sol-6-1-2026-10-01 {"date": "2026-10-01", "what": "The auditor seat moves from gpt-6-sol to gpt-6.1-sol, after the auditor exam on job 1's first diff (.planning/quick/20261001-auditor-exam/RESULT.md): Sol 6.1 at high and xhigh found the blocking defect and two more real ones; Sonnet 5.5 is not seated (at max it let the job pass). Codex CLI upgraded 0.155.1 → 0.159.3 for the model. He also left the EXPLAIN escape found in the exam as it is, and left the board-row approval rule unchanged.", "verbatim": "bence onay işi kalsın olduğu gibi boşver. 3. şıkla iligli. denetçi 6.1 olsun tmm 2.kusur kalsın no prblem.çok ciddi bişey değil.", "conditions": "Critical work stays at xhigh; the floor stays normal.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session cd2a0e9d — heard first-hand, 2026-10-01.", "where": "scripts/governance/codex-refuter.config.toml · refuter.sh · dxb-team2 §2 · dxb-verify · model-routing-hierarchy.md · MODEL_ROUTING_SPEC.md · ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md"}
distrust-rules-deleted-2026-10-01 {"date": "2026-10-01", "what": "Two rules he never gave, both distrusting the lead, are deleted with nothing written in their place: dxb-team2 §3's floor ('a job touching money, the database, security, approval or governance files is at least normal; the lead cannot score it lower' — written by a session on 2026-09-28, e8e05666) and dxb-verify's ruler rule ('every audit's ruler is a runnable script' — grown from the persona ruler of 2026-09-15 into every audit), with the lines that hung on them (the spec/plan-text ruler gap row, 'a class with no ruler gets its ruler first', 'anything machine-catchable the twin finds is recorded as the author's own defect', 'so any later reader can check the lead did not grade itself down'). The card is the lead's judgment; Sol challenges it.", "verbatim": "sil ikisini de. hatta bu şekilde saçma sapan seni engelleyen sana güveni mi sarsan şeyleri de sil.", "conditions": "Lines carrying his own word stay. The entry audit-ruler-is-a-runnable-script-2026-09-15 is history; this order supersedes it.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session dbebfe82 — heard first-hand, 2026-10-01.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md §3 §6 · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md (battery table, ruler table, audit twin) · Codex mirror"}
dxb-verify-battery-and-restart-lines-2026-10-03 {"date": "2026-10-03", "what": "The dxb-verify door's two wrong lines corrected: its check table named `pnpm test` (vitest alone) where the battery is `pnpm construction:battery` (both halves, the sandboxed and the host one); its restart trap said `systemctl --user restart dxb-scheduler dxb-jarvis`, and dxb-jarvis is stopped and disabled — a restart would start it. The trap now restarts dxb-scheduler and says dxb-jarvis is not started.", "verbatim": "dxb-verify düzeltmesine evet", "conditions": "Answering the one-word question carried since session 5ed74ad7 (STATE, 'Waiting on his approval': 'dxb-verify's two-line fix … Recommended: evet'). Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session cbedb76a — heard first-hand, 2026-10-03.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md (the check table's first row, the restart trap) · Codex mirror"}
fable-at-the-end-on-important-jobs-2026-10-04 {"date": "2026-10-04", "what": "Two orders in one sentence. (1) The approved orchestration design is written into dxb-team2 now — the three arrangements and the card's fields (orchestration-three-arrangements-lead-chooses-2026-10-03), a fork or a medium helper writing code under the lead's verification (helpers-write-code-under-lead-verification-2026-10-03; the core's 'Code' sentence and a writing helper seat, helper-writer), Sol's single pass with its findings fixed by a fork or a helper (sol-single-pass-fixes-by-helper-2026-10-03), and the two defects found on the way (the door's dollar figures overwritten when it is opened with a job sentence; the Codex mirror naming hook paths it does not hold). (2) Fable is consulted once per job, at the end — before 'done' — and only on an important job, read as the card's critical class (6-8); in that one call it also rules on a disagreement no test settled. This DELETES (LAW A) the three fixed points of fable-three-checkpoints-2026-10-03 (before a big plan, on a repeated error, before 'done', and 'whenever else the lead needs it') and Fable's ruling on any dispute of a light or normal job — there the lead decides and records why. Sol's single pass is read as one Sol call per job, on the finished work: the critical plan's read by Sol (restored with plan-comes-to-him-once-2026-10-03) and the high-and-xhigh twin audit of the first critical job (paid by the auditor exam of 2026-10-01) are deleted (LAW A). Part (2) — Fable once at the end, on a critical job only — is replaced by his correction of 18:12 the same day, fable-start-and-important-end-2026-10-04 (LAW A).", "verbatim": "4- kalsın gerek yok. diğerlerini tamamla ve bu sistemde fable en sonda sadece önemli konularda danışılsın sanırım şuan hem başta hem de sonda danışılıor galiba ve herşeyde... evet başla!", "conditions": "Set as a /goal in session fd7d67f2, answering the lead's list of 2026-10-04 ~17:13 (items 1, 2, 3, 5; item 4 dropped and written nowhere). 'Önemli konularda' is read by the lead as the critical class; the reading is named to him in the job's report. Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session fd7d67f2 — heard first-hand, 2026-10-04.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md §1-§6, §9 · .claude/CLAUDE.md §2 (Code) · ~/.claude/agents/helper-writer.md · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md · HOLDING-OS-MASTER-PLAN/00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-AUDIT-TWIN.md §4 · scripts/governance/sync-codex-mirror.sh · .planning/quick/20261004-orchestration-door/"}
fable-start-and-important-end-2026-10-04 {"date": "2026-10-04", "what": "Fable 5.1 is consulted only where the job's score card says, measured before it is consulted: at SCORE the lead writes on the card a `fable:` line — `none` · `start` · `start+end` — with its why, and Fable is consulted only where that line says. A light job (0-2): `none`. A normal job (3-5): `start` — once, before the plan goes to the CEO; not at the end. An important job: `start+end`; important is the card's critical class (6-8), or a design, plan or architecture job whose risk axis is 2 (money, database, security, approval, governance, agents). The start call reads the approach, the plan and the design, and the lead closes its gaps; the end call, before 'done', reads the finished work with Sol's findings and in the same call rules on a disagreement no test settled. Nowhere else: not on a repeated error, not 'whenever the lead needs it', not on a light job; the advisor tool's own advice to call it before substantive work or when done applies only where the card's `fable:` line allows it. Disputes: on an important job Fable rules in its end call; otherwise the lead decides and records why. This replaces part (2) of fable-at-the-end-on-important-jobs-2026-10-04 (LAW A): 'en sonda' was a slip for 'başta'. Its point 3 (a normal job: the start only) is replaced by his answer of 19:22 the same day, fable-start-and-end-normal-and-important-2026-10-04 (LAW A).", "verbatim": "Pardon ya o fable'a sonda değil yani başta danışılır sonda danışılmaz diyecektim. Bir de e, önemli kritik konularda danışılır hem başta hem sonda. Yani bazı basit anlatmak istediğim şu bazı basit durumlarda da Hem başta hem sonda her şeyde danışılıyor yani her konuda onu şey ölçmesi lazım danışmadan önce hani önemli bir konuysa önemli bir proje yapılıyorsa tamam mı yani önemli bir plan tasarım yapılıyorsa önemli bir şey yapılıyorsa Fable'a başta ve sonda da sorulsun ama normal işlerde her şeyde de sorulmasın onu diyorum yani hani bunun Bunun ek şey yapılması istiyorum. Nasıl ekleneceği, nasıl e, tam olarak ekleneceği sana kalmış. Bunu tasarlayan sensin planlayan.", "conditions": "His correction of the /goal of ~17:19, said in session fd7d67f2 at 18:12 local; he left the design to the lead ('Nasıl ekleneceği … sana kalmış. Bunu tasarlayan sensin planlayan.'). The five points were told to him in that session and he pasted that reply into session e3574313 with 'şunu unuttum'. One question stays open with him: whether a normal job should have no Fable at the start either (point 3 is read from 'başta danışılır sonda danışılmaz'). Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session fd7d67f2 — heard first-hand, 2026-10-04 18:12 local; registered by session e3574313, the job's lead after the handover, from fd7d67f2's transcript (promptId 0b087333).", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md (description, §1-§4) · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md · Codex mirror"}
fable-start-and-end-normal-and-important-2026-10-04 {"date": "2026-10-04", "what": "Fable 5.1 advises at the start and at the end of a normal (3-5) or critical (6-8) job — the start call before the plan goes to him, the end call before 'done' (the finished work with Sol's findings, ruling there on a disagreement no test settled) — and never on a light (0-2) job; the card's `fable:` line is `none` or `start+end`, measured before Fable is consulted; nowhere else. Fable advises, it never writes. This replaces point 3 of fable-start-and-important-end-2026-10-04 (a normal job: the start only) — LAW A. Its normal job's end call is replaced by his words of 20:58 the same day, fable-normal-start-only-critical-start-end-2026-10-04 (LAW A).", "verbatim": "Fable için de başta ve sonda sorulsun. Advice yapılsın o kadar. Normal işlerde olabilir bir de önemli işlerde. Basit işlerde gerek yok.", "conditions": "His answer to the open question of fd7d67f2 (whether a normal job should have no Fable at the start either), in the same message as his yes to the live bar ('çubuk için tamam evet'). Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session e3574313 — heard first-hand, 2026-10-04 19:22 local.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md (description, §1-§4) · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md · Codex mirror"}
fable-normal-start-only-critical-start-end-2026-10-04 {"date": "2026-10-04", "what": "Fable 5.1 advises by the job's size, read from the card's class: a light job (0-2) never; a normal job (3-5) once, at the start, before the plan goes to him; an important job — the card's critical class (6-8) — at the start and at the end (before 'done', reading the finished work with Sol's findings and ruling there on a disagreement no test settled). The card's `fable:` line is `none` · `start` · `start+end`. This replaces the normal job's end call of fable-start-and-end-normal-and-important-2026-10-04 (LAW A). The audit he describes in the same message is the one already written: one Sol pass, its findings fixed, then the tests (sol-single-pass-fixes-by-helper-2026-10-03). design-eye runs on Fable 5.1 and is bound by the same rule: it reads a finished surface only on a critical job, beside the end call (Sol's single pass on f03dfe16, B1).", "verbatim": "abi küçük işte no fable orta işte başta fable önemli işlerde de başta ve sonra fable olay bu. ben bunu istiyorum. denetimde tek turdu bulunan hatalar tamir edilecekti. ve kontrol. çalışıor mu herşey çalışmıor mu düzgün yapılmış mı diye test sanırım.", "conditions": "Said at 20:58 local in session 89e39ac4, while the lead ran item 4 of the outside review and had named a Fable end call for that normal job under the 19:22 rule. His 'küçük · orta · önemli' are read as the card's light · normal · critical. Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session 89e39ac4 — heard first-hand, 2026-10-04.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md (description, §1, §2 Advisor, §3, §4 PLAN · DISPUTE · JUDGE) · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md (a finding is evidence) · their Codex mirrors · ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (# Danışman) — outside the repo · ~/.claude/agents/design-eye.md (outside the repo)"}
dxb-team2-lean-2026-10-06 {"date": "2026-10-06", "what": "ORDER: dxb-team2 rewritten lean. The lead chooses the hands (itself, a fork, medium helpers, or a fork with helpers) and verifies every piece; one blind Sol pass on every job that changes code, a rule or a door; its findings fixed by a fork or a helper; the touched tests, and the battery once at the end when code changed; a short report. Gone: the score card and audit-card.mjs (refuter.sh takes --effort, high by default, the lead's choice), the done-list, Fable in a dxb-team2 job (the advisor tool and the Fable-based design-eye), per-job records (his words only in this ledger where LAW B needs them; STATE once at the session's end, a few lines). Effort: the session at high; plan, design and architecture at max — he switches, the lead warns him on every reply until he has (.claude/hooks/dxb-effort-warn.py plan|build|off, the live level read from the status line's record). Supersedes score-card-gate-2026-10-01, auditor-never-regrades-2026-10-03 and fable-normal-start-only-critical-start-end-2026-10-04 (LAW A); those entries stay as history. Also fixed on the way, as he asked ('eksik, bozuk şeyler varsa onları da düzelt'): ~/.claude/agents/refuter.md's two older defects (Sol's C1, C2 of 2026-10-04 — a C finding no longer goes to the board; the fallback auditor runs only reading commands), its effort high as the door says.", "verbatim": "Şu an Haydasın ve orkestratörsün. DXP 2, DXP Team 2 tasarla bakalım aynı konuştuğumuz şekilde. Bu şekilde onaylıyorum. Ve tasarlarken eksik, bozuk şeyler varsa onları da düzelt tabii ki. · Ferrari seviyesinde. Seviye Ferrari seviyesi uluslararası yarışmalarda birinciliğe aday olacak bir e, orkestratör sistemi olsun. Konuştuğumuz bu plan dahilinde.", "conditions": "Said after the lead laid out the flow in this conversation (the job → the lead chooses the hands → the work → Sol → the fixes → the tests → a short report; plan talk warned to max, the build to high) and he had switched the session to high himself. 'Haydasın' is the dictation of 'high'dasın', 'DXP Team 2' of dxb-team2. Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session f7a2bf71 — heard first-hand, 2026-10-06.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md · .claude/hooks/dxb-effort-warn.py · .claude/settings.json · scripts/governance/refuter.sh · tests/governance/refuter-gate.test.ts · tests/hooks/effort-warn.test.ts · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md · HOLDING-OS-MASTER-PLAN/MODEL_ROUTING_SPEC.md · ~/.claude/agents/{refuter,helper,helper-writer,design-eye}.md, ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, ~/.claude/hooks/dxb-statusline.js (outside the repo)"}
dxb-team2-overall-look-fixes-2026-10-06 {"date": "2026-10-06", "what": "ORDER, accepting the lead's recommendations after the overall look at dxb-team2: (1) dxb-verify names the fallback refuter's exception — read-only by word, not by tool, named in the report; (2) ~/.claude/agents/debugger.md hands a fix to the lead, a fork or a helper-writer, the builder only for a piece that failed twice at high; (3) the battery runs before Sol, which gets its output, and again after the fixes when a fix changed code. Also, the same day, accepting the recommendation of the Fable-review job: Sol's raw dumps (*.raw) and briefs (*brief*.txt) stay on disk and out of git; SOL.md is committed.", "verbatim": "Önerilerine ilgili hepsi. · Önerin ikincisinde önerini kabul ediyorum.", "conditions": "The first sentence answered the lead's four recommendations (the fourth was only a note that the plan warning has not yet been seen on his screen). The second, earlier, answered the three found items of the Fable-review job, accepting the second. Registered as his order, not a LAW B acceptance.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session f0af511e — heard first-hand, 2026-10-06.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md §1 §4 §5 §6 · .claude/skills/dxb-verify/SKILL.md · ~/.claude/agents/debugger.md (outside the repo) · .gitignore"}
light-lane-small-jobs-opus-medium-2026-11-07 {"date": "2026-11-07", "what": "The light lane, open since 22 Oct, is decided: a small, low-risk job is done end to end by one Opus 5.5 session at medium, tested at once, with no Sol pass; work that would swell its context is handed to a helper. Written into dxb-team2 §1 and §4.", "verbatim": "Yani küçük ve şey küçük ve düşük riskli işler tek şeyle medium'la yapılsın işte, aynen. Mesela biz seninle yaptık yani medium referral'de. Aynen bu şekilde Opus medium'la yapılsın, güzel. Yani önemli olan konteksti şişirmemek, yani başkasına yaptırmak işi devretmek. Yani o konteks şişmemesi lazım yani.", "conditions": "His example: the dictation fix of 2026-11-07. The technical boundary is the engineers'; money, the approval gate, security, moving data, parallel or many-place changes keep the full flow.", "session": "Opus 5.5 session d5674644 — heard first-hand, 2026-11-07.", "where": ".claude/skills/dxb-team2/SKILL.md §1 (the flow) and §4"}

