   100	# ── THE BENCH'S OWN RULER (CEO 2026-09-21: "tezgah kendini temizlesin her zaman
   101	# bu sorunlarla karşılaşmayalım temiz işle ilerleyelim").
   102	#
   103	# A suite that leaves rows behind poisons the next audit, and for months the
   104	# only way to learn that was for a later run to go red for a reason that had
   105	# nothing to do with the code under test — three files did exactly that on
   106	# 2026-09-21, counting work another suite's scheduler had done. So the battery
   107	# now measures itself: every table in the construction engine's public schema
   108	# is counted before and after, and a table that GREW names itself and turns the
   109	# battery red. pg-boss's own schema is excluded — it is the queue's bookkeeping,
   110	# not the company's record.
   111	#
   112	# It measures the CONSTRUCTION engine and nothing else (port 54422).
   113	#
   114	# FOUR THINGS THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS RULER GOT WRONG, each one measured by
   115	# the adversarial pass on the day it was written (2026-09-21):
   116	#   · it compared with `>` and so was blind to SHRINKING — which is the very
   117	#     fault that started this work, a suite deleting another suite's rows;
   118	#   · it counted only the `public` schema, and `dxb_internal.ops_live_issued`
   119	#     grew 0 -> 247 under it while it reported "no suite left a row behind";
   120	#   · it used an inner join, so a table BORN or DROPPED during the run fell
   121	#     silently out of the comparison;
   122	#   · when it could not measure at all it still printed "residue: none" and
   123	#     allowed BATTERY_GREEN — a ruler that cannot see must say so, not agree.
   124	# WHAT IT COUNTS, and the list is deliberate. `public` and `dxb_internal` are
   125	# the schemas this repository's own migrations build — the bench's record of
   126	# the company. Everything else on the engine belongs to somebody else's
   127	# machinery and churns on its own: `pgboss` is the queue's bookkeeping,
   128	# `realtime` grew 642 rows in one run with no suite involved, and `auth`,
   129	# `storage`, `net`, `vault` and the supabase_* schemas are the platform's.
   130	BENCH_URL="${DXB_CONSTRUCTION_URL:-postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54422/postgres}"
   131	bench_counts() {
   132	  local q
   133	  q=$(psql -tA "$BENCH_URL" -c "SELECT string_agg(format('SELECT %L AS t, count(*)::bigint AS n FROM %I.%I', schemaname||'.'||tablename, schemaname, tablename), ' UNION ALL ') FROM pg_tables WHERE schemaname IN ('public','dxb_internal');" 2>/dev/null) || return 1
   134	  [ -z "$q" ] && return 1
   135	  # COLLATE "C" and LC_ALL=C below so the two lists are ordered by the same
   136	  # rule; join needs that, and the server's collation is not the shell's.
   137	  psql -tA -F'|' "$BENCH_URL" -c "SELECT t, n FROM ($q) s ORDER BY t COLLATE \"C\";" 2>/dev/null
   138	}
   139	BEFORE_ROWS="$(PGPASSWORD=postgres bench_counts || true)"
   140	if [ -z "$BEFORE_ROWS" ]; then
   141	  echo "⚠ UNVERIFIED — the bench ruler could not read $BENCH_URL; residue is NOT measured this run"
   142	fi
   143	
   144	echo "=== 1/2 · THE CONSTRUCTION RUNTIME — the sandboxed suite ==="
   145	EXCLUDES=()
   146	for f in "${HOST_FILES[@]}"; do EXCLUDES+=(--exclude "$f"); done
   147	bash scripts/construction/run.sh pnpm vitest run "${EXCLUDES[@]}"
   148	sandboxed=$?
   149	
   150	echo
   151	echo "=== 2/2 · THE AUTHOR'S HAND — on the company's side, outside the sandbox ==="
   152	for f in "${HOST_FILES[@]}"; do echo "    $f"; done
   153	pnpm vitest run "${HOST_FILES[@]}"
   154	host=$?
   155	
   156	echo
   157	echo "=== THE BENCH'S OWN RULER — what this run left behind ==="
   158	# 0 = measured and clean · 1 = measured and dirty · 2 = could not be measured
   159	residue=2
   160	if [ -n "$BEFORE_ROWS" ]; then
   161	  AFTER_ROWS="$(PGPASSWORD=postgres bench_counts || true)"
   162	  if [ -z "$AFTER_ROWS" ]; then
   163	    echo "⚠ UNVERIFIED — the bench could not be re-counted; residue unknown for this run"
   164	  else
   165	    # -a1 -a2: a table that exists on only ONE side is reported too, never
   166	    # dropped. The empty side reads as '-' and the line says so.
   167	    moved=$(join -t'|' -a1 -a2 -e '-' -o '0,1.2,2.2' \
   168	              <(LC_ALL=C sort -t'|' -k1,1 <<<"$BEFORE_ROWS") \
   169	              <(LC_ALL=C sort -t'|' -k1,1 <<<"$AFTER_ROWS") \
   170	            | awk -F'|' '$2 != $3 {
   171	                 if ($2 == "-")      printf "    %-34s (absent) -> %s   table appeared\n", $1, $3;
   172	                 else if ($3 == "-") printf "    %-34s %s -> (absent)   table vanished\n", $1, $2;
   173	                 else                printf "    %-34s %s -> %s  (%+d)\n", $1, $2, $3, $3-$2;
   174	               }')
   175	    if [ -n "$moved" ]; then
   176	      echo "    a suite changed the construction engine — it must leave what it found:"
   177	      echo "$moved"
   178	      residue=1
   179	    else
   180	      echo "    every table is the size it was — no suite left or took a row"
   181	      residue=0
   182	    fi
   183	  fi
   184	fi
   185	
   186	echo
   187	echo "sandboxed suite : exit $sandboxed"
   188	echo "host suite      : exit $host"
   189	case "$residue" in
   190	  0) echo "bench residue   : none" ;;
     1	#!/usr/bin/env bash
     2	# I18N PURITY CHECK — org surface bilingual completeness gate (E6.3 wave 3d).
     3	# Run before any "done" claim that touches CEO-visible org UI. Three checks:
     4	#   1. every live agent has a Turkish title (title_tr)
     5	#   2. every department has a Turkish display name (display_name_tr)
     6	#   3. message dictionaries EN/TR carry identical key sets
     7	# Exit 0 = PASS, 1 = FAIL (with the failing rows listed).
     8	set -euo pipefail
     9	
    10	REPO_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)"
    11	PSQL=(docker exec -i supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS psql -U postgres -d postgres -At)
    12	
    13	fail=0
    14	
    15	agents_missing="$("${PSQL[@]}" -c "SELECT slug FROM agents WHERE employment_status<>'archived' AND role_level IS DISTINCT FROM 'sub_agent' AND (title IS NULL OR title_tr IS NULL);")"
    16	if [ -n "$agents_missing" ]; then
    17	  echo "FAIL agents missing title/title_tr:"; echo "$agents_missing"; fail=1
    18	else
    19	  echo "PASS agents: every live agent titled EN+TR"
    20	fi
    21	
    22	depts_missing="$("${PSQL[@]}" -c "SELECT slug FROM departments WHERE display_name_tr IS NULL;")"
    23	if [ -n "$depts_missing" ]; then
    24	  echo "FAIL departments missing display_name_tr:"; echo "$depts_missing"; fail=1
    25	else
    26	  echo "PASS departments: every department named EN+TR"
    27	fi
    28	
    29	# Projects are CEO-visible cards; heading AND purpose both render (found
    30	# 2026-07-26: purpose had its Turkish leg, the heading did not, so the TR board
    31	# read "HR Sandbox"). Archived projects are out of the CEO's live view.
    32	projects_missing="$("${PSQL[@]}" -c "SELECT slug FROM projects WHERE status <> 'archived' AND (name_tr IS NULL OR purpose_tr IS NULL);")"
    33	if [ -n "$projects_missing" ]; then
    34	  echo "FAIL projects missing name_tr/purpose_tr:"; echo "$projects_missing"; fail=1
    35	else
    36	  echo "PASS projects: every live project named + explained EN+TR"
    37	fi
    38	
    39	# The risk register is CEO-visible too — /gov/risks and every project's Command
    40	# View render the title. Found by the W5.1 audit twin 2026-07-26: three English
    41	# sentences on the Turkish board because `project_risks` had no `title_tr`.
    42	risks_missing="$("${PSQL[@]}" -c "SELECT left(title, 40) FROM project_risks WHERE title_tr IS NULL OR (note IS NOT NULL AND note_tr IS NULL);")"
    43	if [ -n "$risks_missing" ]; then
    44	  echo "FAIL risks missing title_tr:"; echo "$risks_missing"; fail=1
    45	else
    46	  echo "PASS risks: every risk titled + noted EN+TR"
    47	fi
    48	
    49	# W2.6: the holding now writes on the CEO's board itself. A SYSTEM-authored
    50	# message is an i18n surface — a briefing missing its Turkish leg would print an
    51	# English paragraph straight onto the Turkish board, and its thread name would
    52	# sit in the conversation list in the wrong language. Conversation turns (the
    53	# CEO's own words, Hamza's replies) are deliberately single-leg and out of scope.
    54	briefings_missing="$("${PSQL[@]}" -c "
    55	  SELECT 'message ' || m.id FROM chat_messages m
    56	   WHERE m.source = 'briefing' AND (m.content_tr IS NULL OR btrim(m.content_tr) = '')
    57	  UNION ALL
    58	  SELECT 'thread ' || s.id FROM chat_sessions s
    59	   WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM chat_messages m WHERE m.session_id = s.id AND m.source = 'briefing')
    60	     AND (s.title IS NULL OR s.title_tr IS NULL);")"
    61	if [ -n "$briefings_missing" ]; then
    62	  echo "FAIL system-authored chat rows missing a language leg:"; echo "$briefings_missing"; fail=1
    63	else
    64	  echo "PASS briefings: every system-authored chat row carries EN+TR"
    65	fi
    66	
    67	node - <<EOF || fail=1
    68	const en = require("$REPO_DIR/apps/dashboard/messages/en.json");
    69	const tr = require("$REPO_DIR/apps/dashboard/messages/tr.json");
    70	const flat = (o, p = "") =>
    71	  Object.entries(o).flatMap(([k, v]) =>
    72	    typeof v === "object" ? flat(v, p + k + ".") : [p + k]);
    73	const e = flat(en), t = flat(tr);
    74	const diff = e.filter((k) => !t.includes(k)).concat(t.filter((k) => !e.includes(k)));
    75	if (diff.length) { console.log("FAIL dictionary parity, diff:", diff.join(",")); process.exit(1); }
    76	console.log("PASS dictionary parity: en", e.length, "= tr", t.length);
    77	EOF
    78	
    79	[ $fail -eq 0 ] && echo "I18N PURITY: PASS" || { echo "I18N PURITY: FAIL"; exit 1; }
   115	
   116	**LAW A — a live CEO order DELETES what contradicts it** (CEO, 2026-07-30). Not a footnote
   117	beside it, not "superseded but retained". The contradicting text goes, and the report says
   118	what went. Keeping both is how a record starts lying.
   119	
   120	**LAW B — finished ≠ approved** (CEO, 2026-07-30): *"iş tamamlanınca bitti anlamına gelmez,
   121	ben bakmam lazım."* A green battery means the AUTHOR's work is done. Only the CEO's own eye
   122	makes something **accepted**. No record may say approved / accepted / onaylandı / kabul
   123	edildi without an entry in `scripts/governance/ceo-approvals.json` carrying his words and
   124	the date. The battery fails on an unregistered approval claim.
   125	
   126	## 2. The boundaries that never bend
   127	
   128	- **The approval gate.** Money OUT, contracts, ad spend, identity steps and the subjects he
   129	  marks stop at the CEO. Money IN and routine outward communication do not.
   130	- **Ask before any project work.** Nothing in the project starts until he has said so in this
   131	  conversation (CEO 2026-10-01).
   132	- **Do not state as fact what you did not check.** Owner: `00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-MEASURE-NEVER-GUESS.md`.
   133	- **Evidence before done.** A completion claim cites the command and its decisive output. Anything a terminal cannot observe is labelled `⚠ UNVERIFIED — requires
   134	  human-eye confirmation` and listed apart. Door: `dxb-verify`.
   135	- **A fix must not break what stands around it; the tests show it.** Door: `dxb-verify`.
   136	- **Islamic boundaries are constitutional.** CEO-only. Code may refuse its own work against
   137	  them and warns him once; his word after that warning is done once as an exception, the boundary unchanged
   138	  <!-- CEO-OK: b64-q3-decision17-covers-everything-2026-10-14 -->; code may never widen or narrow them.
   139	- **Code: the session writes it; inside `dxb-team2` a fork, a `helper-writer` and the `builder`
   140	  seat write too, every piece verified by the lead before it is committed**
   141	  <!-- CEO-OK: helpers-write-code-under-lead-verification-2026-10-03 -->. Other subagents audit,
   142	  refute and sweep; they never write — and a
   143	  CHECKER session is bound the same way: it measures, instructs and re-measures, it never writes,
   144	  ruler scripts included (the audit law, CEO 2026-09-15
   145	  <!-- CEO-OK: audit-law-checker-only-checks-2026-09-15 -->; door: `dxb-verify`).
   146	- **The plan exists once.** No new spec, no new plan file. A deviation is a registered
   147	  adaptation inside the spec that already owns the contract.
   148	- **What the CEO drops is not written down.** A discussion that ends in *"forget it"* leaves no
   149	  file, no row, no note — **silence is the record.** Only real, ordered, unfinished work is written
   150	  anywhere. The reflex to keep a dropped idea "just in case" is what grew the always-on layer to 27
   151	  pages, and he should never have to be the one who catches it.
   152	- **Nothing becomes a law unless he says "make it a law".** His order, 2026-08-13: *"ben bir şey kanun olsun demeden onu asla kanun yapma bunu yasaklıyorum… ben bir
   153	  kuralı sadece belirli bir session için söylüorm."* **A rule he states is for THAT session only**
   154	  — obey it fully while it runs, and let it die with the session. Writing it into a law file, a
   155	  banner, a skill or a standing order needs his explicit word. He
   156	  authorised this one sentence, and only this one, to be written as a rule. When a session thinks a
   157	  remark deserves to be permanent, it **asks him** in one line; his answer decides. Measured the day
   158	  he gave it: his passing *"write it short"* had been promoted into the rival ledger's permanent
   159	  banner beside his registered orders, and he caught it.
   160	- **Secrets** never enter the repo, a prompt, or any printed output.
   161	
   162	## 3. Language
   163	
   164	Artifacts in English — specs, code, comments, migrations, commit messages, evidence.
   165	Conversation with the CEO in Turkish: the answer first, plain, short. Every CEO-visible surface is 100 % one locale, both
   166	locales at parity. Owner: `00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-LANGUAGE.md`.
   167	
   168	## 4. THE DOORS — open one when the job matches
   169	
   170	| When you are… | Open |
   171	|---|---|
   172	| asked to learn the holding — what is where | `dxb-start` |
   173	| running a job | `dxb-team2` |
   174	| taking a board row from open to closed | `dxb-close-row` |
   175	| about to claim anything is finished | `dxb-verify` |

