    30	
    31	**The browser leg currently needs one thing from the CEO** — automated login is forbidden because
    32	no second factor is enrolled and a form login would enrol one on his account. Until he mints a
    33	session file by hand, the eye leg of an authenticated surface is `⚠ UNVERIFIED` and says so.
    34	Board row **B03-bis**.
    35	
    36	## The design law — his sentence, made binding
    37	
    38	> **"HER PANELIN CANLI OLDUĞU YAŞAYAN BİR HOLDİNG."**
    39	
    40	1. **Every panel reads from a query or shows an honest empty state.** No panel displays a number
    41	   it cannot prove. A rival's goal panel sat frozen at one figure for a whole video while its
    42	   owner spoke nine different numbers; that is the failure we refuse.
    43	2. **Zero is a real answer.** A quiet board says nothing is running and means it. It never
    44	   animates to look busy.
    45	3. **The refusals are visible.** Every pipeline card names the rule it will not break. This
    46	   system has the strongest refusals of anything we have studied and shows him none of them.
    47	4. **Outward actions look different from reads** — the distinction the whole governance rests on
    48	   must be visible at a glance.
    49	5. **No "…" truncation** (CEO ruling 2026-07-18) — shorten at the source.
    50	6. **Both locales, ≥2 widths, no horizontal overflow** — RULE #0, per surface, same turn.
    51	
    52	## His standing rulings about his own screens
    53	
    54	- **The only pre-approved visual element is the left navigation bar and its icons.** Everything
    55	  else is open to redesign, and he has said the current surfaces are far below the systems he
    56	  admires.
    57	- **Progressive disclosure.** He likes dropdowns, hovers and sub-tabs: *"her şey babak gibi ortada
    58	  olmak zorunda değil"*. Long text collapses by default and is beautiful when opened.
    59	- **Business and construction are two different companies.** No build-process file, label, card,
    60	  metric or navigation item appears in the operating interface of the holding. Engineering
    61	  telemetry belongs in a clearly separated machine/admin environment.
    62	- **The business hierarchy is** Command · Finance · Operations · Organization · Intelligence ·
    63	  Governance · System.
    64	- **Every click leads somewhere.** A card that opens nothing is a defect, not a placeholder.
    65	- **Every timestamp carries its date.**
    66	- **Charts are required where they explain real business information** — and forbidden where they
    67	  do not. Each chart reads a named view and shows an honest empty state.
    68	- **Luxury is a quality standard, not a decorative theme.** "Burj Al Arab" was one throwaway
    69	  example he gave at the start and it must not be treated as the goal. The visual language is the
    70	  Iron Man / JARVIS cockpit; champagne over obsidian; no coffee tones.
    71	- **He approves the design before it is built.** *"Önce bana örnek design sunulacak, gerçeğe
    72	  geçmeden önce. Beğenmediğimi asla onaylamam."* A visual package — every major page, every state
    73	  — comes before implementation. This is not bureaucracy: a working visual is the most precise
    74	  specification a builder can be given.
    75	
    76	## Opus 5.5's default looks — a prompting aid, not his ruling
    77	
    78	Anthropic's Opus 5.5 migration guide ("Frontend design defaults"): left without direction, the
    79	model falls back on a few default looks. None of them is this holding's unless his approved design
    80	shows it — a cream or off-white page, italic accent words in headlines, numbered "01 / 02 / 03"
    81	section labels, pill-shaped buttons (the design system keeps full rounding for avatars and status
    82	dots, `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md:76`). When a draft falls back on another default, add it to this list,
    83	never to his rulings above.
    84	
    85	## Cleaning up after a design pass
    86	
    87	Any demo mutation made to photograph a state is reverted through the same control function that
    88	made it, and the residue is measured to zero. Background collectors and probe processes are swept.
     1	---
     2	name: dxb-persona
     3	description: Use when writing, correcting or filing an employee persona — the authorship rule, the section grammar, the quality gate, the sync path, and the delivery contract a persona must satisfy to reach the live agent.
     4	---
     5	
     6	# Writing an employee
     7	
     8	A persona is not a document. It is a live employee's mind, and 199 of them are the largest
     9	unclaimed asset in this holding.
    10	
    11	## Authorship
    12	
    13	Every persona is written **personally and inline by the session's authorized author** — whichever
    14	model runs the session. A subagent may not write one, even a subagent running the same
    15	model. The HR factory does not author a first-generation persona.
    16	
    17	The database enforces it: `personas_author_check` accepts `opus-5 | fable-5 | hr-factory` only,
    18	and `scripts/sync-personas-to-db.sh` requires `DXB_PERSONA_AUTHOR` with **no default** — a silent
    19	wrong author is worse than a stopped script. Historical rows keep their original author: guessing
    20	which past rows were mislabelled would replace one wrong record with another.
    21	
    22	## Shape
    23	
    24	Sections `## 1.` … `## 12.`, plus `## 13.` where the CEO has bound a specific character to a
    25	specific role. §12 (Discipline DNA & Islamic conduct) is constitutional — one canonical text,
    26	identical in all 199, and the single registered exception to the role-specific-depth rule. §13 is
    27	**not** inherited; it belongs to the name and the trust behind it.
    28	
    29	Section 13 is registered as **optional** in the compiler: making it required would have failed the
    30	other 198 personas at the gate, and omitting it from the section list would have let an authored
    31	section be silently dropped from the compiled prompt.
    32	
    33	## Quality — the CEO's standard, not a template
    34	
    35	Generic, copied or lazy personas are forbidden by his direct order. Zero invention: no fabricated
    36	name, no invented history, no borrowed biography. Marketing and Sales personas carry sales DNA;
    37	every persona carries a proactivity DNA. A department cannot be activated while its personas are
    38	still first-generation.
    39	
    40	**The trap he named himself:** *"Burj Al Arab was one throwaway example I gave at the start — and
    41	it got written into the design department's persona as if it were the goal."* A construction-time
    42	example frozen into a permanent instruction is a defect. When you touch personas, sweep for the
    43	class, not the instance (board row C41).
    44	
    45	## Filing it
    46	
    47	1. Write the file under `personas/<department>/<slug>.md` — the file is the source of authorship;
    48	   the database is runtime and gate.
    49	2. Run the mechanical gate; a missing required section fails it.
    50	3. Sync with the author variable set explicitly.
    51	4. Sign the deep verdict yourself. A gate PASS is not a verdict.
    52	
    53	## Delivery — the half that was missed for three weeks
    54	
    55	A persona that is authored, gated, versioned and stored is worth nothing until the live agent
    56	receives it. The boundary is the `# PERSONA — ` header; the body from there to the end of file is
    57	the identity, and it crosses whole. The dossier table above that header is never sent.
    58	
    59	`tests/r31/persona-delivery.test.ts` fails if any authored section does not arrive, if the dossier
    60	leaks in, or if the last section is lost — a truncating loader passes a "contains §1" check and
    61	fails that one.
    62	
    63	Door `dxb-hamza-context` owns what an agent is told **besides** its persona.

